ID: B3-Ch09c-Upwards
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b3_ch9_consolation,+1) if (v_b3_ch9_currents == 1 && v_is_dead == 0 && v_perception < 3 && v_reflexes < 3)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_b3_ch9_currents == 1 && v_perception >= 3 || v_b3_ch9_currents == 1 && v_reflexes >= 3 || v_b3_ch9_currents == 0)
set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_aura_hardening == 0 && v_b3_ch9_currents == 1 && v_perception < 3 && v_reflexes < 3 || v_b3_ch9_currents == 1 && v_aura_hardening > 0 && v_perception < 3 && v_reflexes < 3)
#if(v_b3_ch9_currents == 0) {
 I shift my physical awareness in Ollendor and raise both arms. Melindra's standard air currents engage instantly, lifting my earthen frame into the gale.

The storm winds hammer my chest, making maneuvering rough, but the magical lift responds with immediate precision. Without Melindra awake to co-pilot, the responsive configuration is far easier to handle.

I circle above the ruins for twenty seconds to dial in my control. Flying through an active storm feels less like swimming and more like wrestling a gnomish glider in a gale, but the currents obey every twitch of my shoulders.

Satisfied, I bank hard toward the lead sentinel. I draw the crossbow from my pack with one hand and put three steel bolts into the golem's iron brow.

"Hey!" I shout over the thunder. "Over here, scrap-heap!"

Two more bolts ring off its jaw. The sentinel halts, massive gears grinding as its head swivels upward. Its iron jaws part, a deep orange glow gathering in its throat.

I break into erratic zigzag evasions to spoil its tracking. The golem discharges a searing beam of fire. It misses, then another tears through the rain, then a third. Each shot shaves closer to my path. The targeting array is calculating my evasion pattern.

A thermal lance sears past my ribs, close enough to scorch wool.

My pulse hammers against my collarbone. Erratic flight is failing; the machine adapts to every roll and bank.

If I maintain a trajectory, it predicts the vector. But if I hover motionless and dodge only at the point of discharge, can I clear the blast radius?

Another beam shears past my shoulder. The math works: at this range, the projectile speed allows a split-second window between the muzzle flash and the burn.

I kill my forward momentum and hover in place, arms spread wide.

"Right here!" I yell into the downpour. "Target locked! Take the shot!"

A heartbeat of silence. The golem's throat flashes. I snap the currents sideways the instant the fire erupts. The beam roars through empty air.

I stabilize twenty feet higher, grinning down at the metal hulk.

"Close!" I shout. "Try again!"

The jaws ignite; I drop two yards on the flash, and the flame punches overhead into the storm clouds. The golem freezes, its glowing eyes locked on my position, mechanical processors completely stalled by a stationary target that moves only on the trigger.

We lock eyes across the rain. Then, a squat, armored blur tears down the street toward the sentinel's flanks at breakneck speed.

}
#if(v_b3_ch9_currents == 1 && v_perception >= 3) {
 I shift my physical awareness in Ollendor and raise both arms. Melindra's heavy currents engage, lifting my earthen frame into the downpour.

The lift is sluggish. Without Melindra awake to manage the secondary flows, the specialized matrix lacks its usual snap. The single advantage is mass: the dense current holds its line against the gale without drifting.

I climb above the shattered masonry and angle toward the lead sentinel. I draw my crossbow and sink three bolts into the brass plating above its eye slits.

"Hey!" I shout. "Over here, scrap-heap!"

I loose two more bolts against its collar. The machine stops, its iron head grinding around to face me. The jaws unhinge, heat gathering in its core.

I begin sweeping evasive arcs, but the sluggish currents make tight turns impossible. The golem fires. A fire beam scorches the air to my left. A second shot cuts closer. A third boils the rainwater off my boots.

The machine is reading my drift.

With the heavy currents, split-second course corrections are out of the question. I need an earlier tell.

On the fourth shot, I catch it: three frames before the throat ignites, the automaton's neck tilts two degrees to the left.

The firing tell.

I maintain a steady, lazy drift. The moment the chin tilts, I throw all my weight in the opposite direction. The fire beam burns empty space where I was about to drift. The golem pauses, re-aligns, and tilts its chin again; I cut hard the other way.

After four consecutive misses against an ostensibly predictable target, the sentinel's joints lock up, its processors stalled in an analytical loop.

We hang in the rain, staring each other down. Then, a squat, armored blur tears across the rubble below, closing on the golem at blinding speed.

}
#if(v_b3_ch9_currents == 1 && v_aura_hardening >= 0 && v_perception < 3 || v_b3_ch9_currents == 1 && v_reflexes >= 3 && v_perception < 3) {
 I shift my physical awareness in Ollendor and raise both arms. Melindra's heavy currents engage, lifting my earthen frame into the downpour.

The lift is sluggish. Without Melindra awake to manage the secondary flows, the specialized matrix lacks its usual snap. The single advantage is mass: the dense current holds its line against the gale without drifting.

I climb above the shattered masonry and angle toward the lead sentinel. I draw my crossbow and sink three bolts into the brass plating above its eye slits.

"Hey!" I shout. "Over here, scrap-heap!"

I loose two more bolts against its collar. The machine stops, its iron head grinding around to face me. The jaws unhinge, heat gathering in its core.

}
#if(v_b3_ch9_currents == 1 && v_reflexes >= 3 && v_perception < 3) {
 I weave through the storm, but the sluggish currents cannot outpace the sentinel's targeting array. Each beam shears closer than the last. Heat washes over my face as a third lance boils the rain off my collar.

I cannot out-maneuver the machine on flight mechanics alone. I have to rely on raw reaction time.

I kill my momentum and hang in mid-air, waving my arms.

"Come on!" I shout into the rain. "I am right here! Take the shot!"

The throat flares. My nerves fire on the flash, muscles jerking me clear a split-second before the beam tears the air.

I brake twenty feet higher.

"What is the matter?" I yell. "Algorithm can't handle a target that doesn't move until you pull the trigger?"

The jaws ignite again; I drop like a stone on the flash, and the fire screams overhead. The golem lowers its head, confused servos whining as its prediction model collapses.

I hang in the storm, waiting. Below, a squat, armored blur tears across the ruins at incredible speed.

}
#if(v_aura_hardening == 0 && v_b3_ch9_currents == 1 && v_perception < 3 && v_reflexes < 3) {
 I attempt to weave through the storm, but the sluggish currents cannot break the sentinel's lock. Each shot closes the margin.

The heavy matrix lags on my command. The next beam catches me center-mass, and the fire incinerates flesh and bone in a fraction of a second.

}
#if(v_b3_ch9_currents == 1 && v_aura_hardening > 0 && v_perception < 3 && v_reflexes < 3) {
 I attempt to weave through the storm, but the sluggish currents cannot break the sentinel's lock. Each shot closes the margin.

The heavy matrix lags on my command. The next beam catches me center-mass, burning straight through my hardened aura and turning me to ash.

}
