I cannot break line of sight with all four sentinels at once, but positioning between two of them prevents them from opening fire without destroying each other.

I drop into an alley between the lead pair, keeping a ruined tenement wall between myself and the third. That leaves only one firing vector to monitor.

I blink to the ether, anchoring another magic pillar while tracking the fourth sentinel from the corner of my eye.

The golem to my left recalculates, deciding that incinerating its fellow unit is an acceptable trade to eliminate me, and opens fire without hesitation.

#if(v_b3_ch9_currents == 0 && v_reflexes < 2) {
 The delay in shifting focus to my earthen limbs costs me the fraction of a second I need to clear the arc. The thermal beam engulfs me, burning flesh to ash before I can react.

